# rows and config keys"): each switch a row's install function hands its module (forced on, forced off), each row's phase, switch key, switch member and
# end step, the documented order of the rows (the first row moved just after the second), ScopeNormal()'s reader list (a non-reader added, the off
# answer), and every field LogConfig writes by hand. Every mutant replaces one whole line (or, for an order mutant, moves one row), and is judged by
# combat_install_test (build/quest-host-combat). combat_install.cpp is a shared file: run this list in a scratch copy of the tree (git archive), never
# in the shared checkout, or hold the port2 shared lock for the whole run. Sourced by ../mutants.sh, which defines
# `runm <name> <file> <sed> [<dir> <target>]`.
